From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:04:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fs-proc-task_mmu-pin-mm_users-in-do_pagemap_scan-fix

remove unneeded & undesirable test for !mm

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Jann Horn <jannh@google.com>
Cc: Liam R. Howlett <liam@infradead.org>
Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>
Cc: Muhammad Usama Anjum <usama.anjum@arm.com>
Cc: Ngoc Quy <ngocquy0700@gmail.com>
Cc: Pedro Falcato <pfalcato@suse.de>
Cc: Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@kernel.org>
---
 fs/proc/task_mmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/proc/task_mmu.c b/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
index 435288824fb02..7452b695fdaec 100644
--- a/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
+++ b/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
@@ -3120,7 +3120,7 @@ static long do_pagemap_scan(struct mm_struct *mm, unsigned long uarg)
 	size_t n_ranges_out = 0;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!mm || !mmget_not_zero(mm))
+	if (!mmget_not_zero(mm))
 		return -ESRCH;
 
 	ret = pagemap_scan_get_args(&p.arg, uarg);
-- 
2.47.3

